      "metadata": {
        "id": "WNoVEPC_oVOC"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Part 4: Inference (Testing the Translator)\n",
        "\n",
        "Now use your fine-tuned model to translate new sentences using the `pipeline` utility."
      ],
      "id": "WNoVEPC_oVOC"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a-vGhjZaoVOD"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Test with new sentences\n",
        "text1 = \"Hello, how are you doing today?\"\n",
        "text2 = \"The transformer model is a powerful architecture for NLP.\"\n",
        "text3 = \"This assignment is for my machine learning lab.\"\n"
      ],
      "id": "a-vGhjZaoVOD"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oQzZ2HWuoVOD"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Part 5: Comparative Analysis (Transformer vs. LSTM)\n",
        "\n",
        "In this section, you will directly compare the output of your new Transformer model with the LSTM-based model from your previous lab.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5.1. Test Sentences\n",
        "Here is a list of 10 English sentences varying in length and complexity."
      ],
      "id": "oQzZ2HWuoVOD"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yUplYFRUoVOE"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "test_sentences = [\n",
        "    # 1. Simple sentence\n",
        "    \"The cat sat on the mat.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 2. Longer sentence\n",
        "    \"I am going to the library to read a book.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 3. Question\n",
        "    \"What is your favorite color?\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 4. Long-range dependency\n",
        "    \"The man who lives down the street just bought a new car.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 5. Figurative language (often difficult)\n",
        "    \"It's raining cats and dogs outside.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 6. Technical term\n",
        "    \"The machine learning model was trained on a large dataset.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 7. Command\n",
        "    \"Please close the door when you leave.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 8. Classic test sentence\n",
        "    \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 9. Negation\n",
        "    \"He did not want to go to the party.\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 10. Future tense\n",
        "    \"We will travel to Germany next summer.\"\n",
        "]\n"
      ],
      "id": "yUplYFRUoVOE"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "z6nk_0RQoVOE"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 5.2. Translation and Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "**Your Task:**\n",
        "1.  **Generate Transformer Translations:** Run the code cell above to get the Transformer's translations.\n",
        "2.  **Generate LSTM Translations:** Load your saved LSTM model and tokenizer from the previous lab. Use it to translate the same 10 above `test_sentences`.\n",
        "3.  **Create Comparison Table:** **Double-click this text cell** to edit it. Fill in the table below with your models' outputs.\n",
        "\n",
        "| # | Original English | LSTM Translation (Previous Lab) | Transformer Translation (This Lab) |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| 1 | The cat sat on the mat. | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 2 | I am going to the library... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 3 | What is your favorite color?| *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 4 | The man who lives down... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 5 | It's raining cats and dogs... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 6 | The machine learning model...| *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 7 | Please close the door... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 8 | The quick brown fox... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 9 | He did not want to go... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |\n",
        "| 10| We will travel to Germany... | *... (Your LSTM's output)* | *... (Your Transformer's output)* |"
      ],
      "id": "z6nk_0RQoVOE"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "87tieEGwoVOE"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Part 6: Visualizing Attention Mechanisms\n",
        "\n",
        "The key difference between your LSTM model (which may have used basic *cross-attention*) and the Transformer is the Transformer's use of **self-attention**.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Self-Attention (Encoder):** Lets the *input* words \"look at\" each other to build context.\n",
        "* **Cross-Attention (Decoder):** Lets the *output* words \"look at\" the input words (this is what your LSTM model also did).\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Get Model Outputs for Visualization\n",
        "We must load the model again from the saved path, this time telling it to `output_attentions`."
      ],
      "id": "87tieEGwoVOE"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MCjUn8EaoVOF"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [],
      "id": "MCjUn8EaoVOF"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bLhxNJnEoVOF"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 2. Visualize Encoder Self-Attention (Input-to-Input)\n",
        "This shows how the English sentence understands its own grammar.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Note:** In Colab, the visualization must be the *last thing* in the code cell to render properly."
      ],
      "id": "bLhxNJnEoVOF"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LdwnS86ZoVOF"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [],
      "id": "LdwnS86ZoVOF"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tzpYbkQ_oVOG"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 3. Visualize Encoder-Decoder Cross-Attention (Target-to-Input)\n",
        "This shows how the model translates, aligning German words to English words. This is the part analogous to your LSTM's attention."
      ],
      "id": "tzpYbkQ_oVOG"
